{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UNuYE7e8qrzAcG7BsCz7hb","type":"tool_result","content":"# Scope, context, and exploration tools (TS)\n\n`src/scope/` (public surface in `index.ts`), `src/context/`,\n`src/snapshot/`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Every `git diff` argument list starts with `DIFF_CONFIG` (use\n  `diffArgs(...)` in `src/scope/git.ts`); git rejects an empty\n  `diff.orderFile=`, so it is `/dev/null`.\n- Patch output goes through `gitPatch` (streams into a\n  `SectionCapper`), never the buffered runner.\n- `build` takes the git environment as `BuildOpts.env` (the CLI\n  context's env).\n- The secret denylist lives once in `src/snapshot/denylist.ts`; scope,\n  context, and snapshot import it.\n- Repo survey (`scope: \"repo\"`) is `src/scope/survey.ts`: it lists the\n  HEAD tree with `ls-tree` and filters in process (`untrackedPasses`,\n  exact-match linguist set), so the git pathspec is unused there. Every\n  repository-derived string in the manifest goes through\n  `manifestQuote`. The CLI survey branches live in `src/cli/review.ts`;\n  CLI tests are in `test/cli/review-survey.ts`.\n\n## Context\n\n- Every function that runs git or reads files takes a trailing\n  `ContextOpts` (`signal`, `env`); pass the CLI context's env, and the\n  repo env in tests. `pinIndexTree` reads `GIT_INDEX_FILE` from that\n  env, not `process.env`.\n- Blocking git calls use the shared runner; streamed reads use\n  `gitStream` / `gitCapped` (`src/context/git.ts`).\n- Grounding and normalization work on `Buffer`s; decode to text only in\n  `snippet.ts` (model-facing).\n- Exploration tools (`src/context/tools.ts`): `explorationTools(repo,\n  tree, {env})`; each `run(args, signal)` returns a plain object, a\n  model-caused failure is `{error}`, abort rejects.\n- When stopping a `gitStream` early, `await lineReader.close()` before\n  awaiting `done`: a paused stdout keeps the child's `close` from\n  firing.\n\n## Snapshot\n\n- `src/snapshot/snapshot.ts` owns `liveIndexPath` and `copyIndex`;\n  `pinIndexTree` (context) uses them too. Every function takes\n  `{env, signal}`; pass the CLI context's env so `GIT_INDEX_FILE` is\n  read from it.\n- `review.ts` keeps a `durable` flag: until the run record is\n  initialized, the `finally` deletes a captured ref. Code added between\n  capture and `initializeRun` stays inside that `try`.\n- Non-staged reviews read the `pinWorktree` tree even with\n  `review.snapshot: false`; only a pin failure falls back to the live\n  tree.\n- `restore` and `removeWorktree` strip `GIT_INDEX_FILE` from the env\n  they are given (deliberate change 12); other functions honor it.\n- `prune` takes fractional milliseconds: `runs prune` converts the Go\n  duration without truncating, so `--older-than 1ns` stays positive\n  instead of falling back to 30 days.\n- `runs checkout` resolves a relative `dir` against `ctx.cwd`, not\n  `process.cwd()`; CLI tests chdir into the repo, so a test from a\n  subdirectory passes `cwd` to `r.roast` to tell them apart.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Use `newRepo()` (`test/scope/helpers.ts`): a temp repo with its own\n  HOME, XDG_CONFIG_HOME, and `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` file\n  (`repo.globalConfig`, safe to fill with hostile config), passed as\n  `env:repo.env`.\n- APFS refuses non-UTF-8 file names; stage such a name with\n  `git update-index --index-info` to test it on macOS.\n- Memory bounds: plain RSS growth reflects V8 GC timing on discarded\n  pipe chunks, not what code keeps alive. `test/scope/huge.ts` forces gc\n  (`v8.setFlagsFromString('--expose-gc')`, `vm.runInNewContext('gc')`)\n  and bounds `heapUsed + external`.\n- Abort tests put a pid-recording fake `git` first on the env's `PATH`\n  (`wrapGit` in `test/context/bounds.ts`).\n- Tool tests call tools through `call(repo, tree, name, args)` and fake\n  git with `fakeGit` / `onArg` (`test/context/tools-helpers.ts`).\n- Snapshot module tests use the \"messy repo\" fixture in\n  `test/snapshot/snapshot.ts` (copied in `test/snapshot/restore.ts`).\n  A restore failure after `worktree add` is provoked with a hand-made\n  ref whose `worktree` entry is a blob. Tests that check out a worktree\n  remove it with `git worktree remove --force` in `t.cleanup`. CLI snapshot tests turn capture on with\n  `review:{}` (settingsRepo disables it) and read refs with\n  `for-each-ref refs/roast/snapshots/`.\n- `npm run test:one` pipes into tap-spec, which can crash with EPIPE on\n  a failing assertion and hide the summary; rerun the bundle with\n  `node test/one-bundle.js` for raw TAP.\n- Captured-worktree tests build the tree with plumbing (temporary\n  `GIT_INDEX_FILE`, `read-tree HEAD`, `add`, `write-tree`). `write-tree`\n  or `status` on the live index rewrites it, so snapshot the index bytes\n  after those calls when asserting it is unchanged.\n# TypeScript\n\nApplies to `src/`, `test/`, and `scripts/`. Notes for one area are in\nthat area's file (index in `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Tooling\n\n- `npm test` builds `dist/cli.js`, then bundles and runs the tapzero\n  suite; it does not typecheck. A new test module must be imported from\n  `test/index.ts`. esbuild drops unused imports without resolving them,\n  so only `npm run typecheck` catches a broken import.\n- `npm run test:one -- test/<area>/<file>.ts` bundles one test module\n  to `test/one-bundle.js` and runs it through tap-spec. Test modules\n  cannot run directly under Node: their `.js` import specifiers only\n  resolve once bundled. It does not typecheck; run `typecheck` too.\n- Lint with `npm run lint`: it preloads `scripts/eslint-ts6.ts`, which\n  gives eslint the TypeScript 6 API because typescript-eslint throws on\n  the TypeScript 7 that `typecheck` uses.\n- Node runs `scripts/` directly (type stripping), so they use only\n  erasable syntax: no enums, namespaces, or parameter properties.\n- `baseOptions` in `scripts/esbuild-options.ts` holds the esbuild\n  options every bundle shares (text loaders for `.tmpl`, `.md`, `.sh`;\n  `mainFields: ['module', 'main']`, which `jsonc-parser`'s UMD build\n  needs); `scripts/bundle.ts` adds the `require` shim banner. A test\n  that bundles code itself uses both.\n- `npm run build` also writes `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`\n  (`scripts/licenses.ts`) and fails, naming the package, when a bundled\n  package lacks an allowlisted `license` field or a license file. A new\n  runtime library must pass it; extending `ALLOWED_LICENSES` needs\n  maintainer approval. `@substrate-system/debug` fails it today, so no\n  `src/` module may import it yet. Runtime libraries are\n  `devDependencies` (bundled); `dependencies` stays empty.\n\n## Source conventions\n\n- Keep source ASCII: write `\\uXXXX` escapes. Some editing tools decode\n  escapes into literal characters when writing; check with\n  `grep -nP '[^\\x00-\\x7f]'` after writing a file. eslint `--fix`\n  (quote-props) rewrites a quoted `'\\u00e9'` object key into a literal\n  non-ASCII identifier; put such keys in a const and use a computed key.\n- eslint rejects control characters in regex literals\n  (`no-control-regex`) and labeled statements (`no-labels`); scan char\n  codes and use helper functions instead.\n- Startup guards live in `src/startup.ts`, not `src/cli.ts`: importing\n  the entry runs the CLI, so testable helpers sit in other modules.\n- Module-level swappable functions use a mutable hooks object plus a\n  delegating export (`terminalHooks`, `skillHooks.lookPath`), because\n  tests cannot reassign an ESM `let` export. Swap the object's field\n  and restore it in `t.cleanup`.\n- Shared helpers; import these, never re-implement:\n  `src/gocompat/` (`strings.ts`: Go TrimSpace/Ext/`%.2f`/strconv.Quote/\n  byte-order sort and `truncateUtf8`; `duration.ts`: Go durations as\n  bigint nanoseconds; `match.ts`: Go `path.Match`),\n  `src/textsafe/textsafe.ts`, `src/fsutil/atomic.ts`\n  (`writeFileAtomic`, options cover trust, credentials, and gate temp\n  names and error messages), `src/git/git.ts` (the only git runner;\n  pass the CLI context's `env`, it reads `process.env` only when none is\n  given), `src/util/pool.ts` (`mapPool`).\n\n// The secret denylist (spec 11, \"Secret denylist\"): untracked paths that\n// are never folded into a review diff, captured into a snapshot, or\n// served from the live working tree.\nimport { goPathMatch } from '../gocompat/match.js'\nimport { git } from '../git/git.js'\nimport { compareBytes, decodePaths } from '../scope/text.js'\n\n// SSH keys match by key-type prefix so suffixed names are covered; a bare\n// `id_*` would also drop ordinary sources such as id_map.go.\nexport const DEFAULT_DENYLIST:readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\n    '.env*', '*.pem', '*_rsa', '*.key', 'creds*',\n    'id_rsa*', 'id_dsa*', 'id_ecdsa*', 'id_ed25519*', 'id_xmss*',\n    'credentials.json', '.npmrc', '.pypirc', '.netrc', '_netrc', '.pgpass',\n    '.git-credentials', '*.p12', '*.pfx',\n])\n\nfunction basename (p:string):string {\n    const i = p.lastIndexOf('/')\n    return i === -1 ? p : p.slice(i + 1)\n}\n\n// Whether a repo-relative `/`-separated path matches any pattern, by its\n// basename or its full path, case-insensitively. A malformed pattern\n// never matches.\nexport function denylisted (\n    path:string,\n    patterns:readonly string[] = DEFAULT_DENYLIST\n):boolean {\n    const full = path.toLowerCase()\n    const base = basename(full)\n    return patterns.some(pattern => {\n        const p = pattern.toLowerCase()\n        return goPathMatch(p, base) || goPathMatch(p, full)\n    })\n}\n\nexport interface DenylistedUntrackedOpts {\n    // Omitted means DEFAULT_DENYLIST; an empty list disables filtering.\n    patterns?:readonly string[];\n    signal?:AbortSignal;\n    env?:NodeJS.ProcessEnv;\n}\n\n// The untracked, non-ignored paths matching the denylist, in byte order.\n// Tracked files are never listed: their content is already in history.\nexport async function denylistedUntracked (\n    repo:string,\n    opts:DenylistedUntrackedOpts = {}\n):Promise<string[]> {\n    const patterns = opts.patterns ?? DEFAULT_DENYLIST\n    if (patterns.length === 0) return []\n    const out = await git(repo,\n        ['ls-files', '--others', '--exclude-standard', '-z'],\n        { signal:opts.signal, env:opts.env })\n    return decodePaths(out).paths\n        .filter(p => p !== '' && denylisted(p, patterns))\n        .sort(compareBytes)\n}\n    fn:(dir:string) => Promise<T>\n):Promise<T> {\n    let tmp:string\n    try {\n        tmp = await fs.mkdtemp(path.join(os.tmpdir(), prefix))\n    } catch (err) {\n        throw wrap('temp dir', err)\n    }\n    try {\n        return await fn(tmp)\n    } finally {\n        await fs.rm(tmp, { recursive:true, force:true })\n    }\n}\n\n// Pin steps 3-7 inside `tmp`: the worktree written through a private\n// copy of the live index, with denylisted untracked paths excluded.\nasync function writeWorktree (\n    repo:string,\n    live:string,\n    tmp:string,\n    opts:PinOptions\n):Promise<Pin> {\n    const idx = path.join(tmp, 'worktree')\n    await copyIndex(live, idx)\n    const excluded = await denylistedUntracked(repo, {\n        patterns:opts.denylist, signal:opts.signal, env:opts.env,\n    })\n    const env = { GIT_INDEX_FILE:idx }\n    // The positive `.` is required: an exclude-only pathspec matches\n    // nothing. `literal` keeps metacharacters in names from widening.\n    const args = ['add', '-A', '--', '.',\n        ...excluded.map(p => `:(exclude,literal)${p}`)]\n    await step('git add -A (snapshot index)', opts,\n        () => run(repo, args, opts, { env }))\n    const tree = await step('write-tree (worktree)', opts,\n        () => run(repo, ['write-tree'], opts, { env }))\n    return { tree, excluded }\n}\n\n// Writes the working tree, as a review sees it, into one unreferenced\n// tree object. Needs no HEAD and leaves the live index untouched.\nexport async function pinWorktree (\n    repo:string,\n    opts:PinOptions = {}\n):Promise<Pin> {\n    const gitDir = await gitDirOf(repo, opts)\n    const live = liveIndexPath(repo, gitDir, opts.env ?? process.env)\n    return withTempDir('roast-pin-',\n        tmp => writeWorktree(repo, live, tmp, opts))\n}\n\n// Records a replayable snapshot: index and worktree trees joined in one\n// composite tree, committed on HEAD (and a differing base), and pointed\n// at by refs/roast/snapshots/<runId>. Throws rather than returning a\n// partial snapshot.\nexport async function capture (\n    repo:string,\n    opts:CaptureOptions\n):Promise<Snapshot> {\n    if (opts.runId === '') throw new Error('snapshot: empty run id')\n    if (opts.headOid === '') {\n        throw new Error('repository has no commits; an unborn HEAD ' +\n            'cannot be restored, so no replayable snapshot is possible')\n    }\n    const gitDir = await gitDirOf(repo, opts)\n    const live = liveIndexPath(repo, gitDir, opts.env ?? process.env)\n    return withTempDir('roast-snapshot-', async tmp => {\n        let indexTree = opts.indexTree ?? ''\n        if (indexTree === '') {\n            const idx = path.join(tmp, 'index')\n            await copyIndex(live, idx)\n            indexTree = await step('write-tree (index)', opts,\n                () => run(repo, ['write-tree'], opts,\n                    { env:{ GIT_INDEX_FILE:idx } }))\n        }\n        const worktree = opts.worktree?.tree ?\n            opts.worktree :\n            await writeWorktree(repo, live, tmp, opts)\n        const composite = await step('mktree', opts, () => run(repo,\n            ['mktree'], opts, {\n                input:`040000 tree ${indexTree}\\tindex\\n` +\n                    `040000 tree ${worktree.tree}\\tworktree\\n`,\n            }))\n        const parents = ['-p', opts.headOid]\n        if (opts.baseOid !== '' && opts.baseOid !== opts.headOid) {\n            parents.push('-p', opts.baseOid)\n        }\n        const commit = await step('commit-tree', opts, () => run(repo,\n            ['commit-tree', composite, ...parents,\n                '-m', `roast run ${opts.runId}`],\n            opts, { env:IDENTITY }))\n        const ref = REF_PREFIX + opts.runId\n        await step(`update-ref ${ref}`, opts,\n            () => run(repo, ['update-ref', ref, commit], opts))\n        return {\n            ref,\n            commit,\n            indexTree,\n            worktreeTree:worktree.tree,\n            head:opts.headOid,\n            base:opts.baseOid,\n            excluded:[...worktree.excluded],\n        }\n    })\n}\n\n// Deletes a run's snapshot ref (the review's cleanup before its run\n// record exists).\nexport async function deleteSnapshot (\n    repo:string,\n    runId:string,\n    opts:SnapshotOpts = {}\n):Promise<void> {\n    if (runId === '') throw new Error('delete snapshot: empty run id')\n    const ref = REF_PREFIX + runId\n    await step(`delete ${ref}`, opts,\n        () => run(repo, ['update-ref', '-d', ref], opts))\n}\n\nasync function verify (\n    repo:string,\n    rev:string,\n    opts:SnapshotOpts\n):Promise<string> {\n    try {\n        return await run(repo,\n            ['rev-parse', '--verify', '--quiet', '--end-of-options', rev],\n            opts)\n    } catch {\n        opts.signal?.throwIfAborted()\n        return ''\n    }\n}\n\n// A snapshot from its ref alone: trees from the composite, head and base\n// from the commit's parents (best effort). `excluded` is not recoverable.\nexport async function load (\n    repo:string,\n    runId:string,\n    opts:SnapshotOpts = {}\n):Promise<Snapshot> {\n    const ref = REF_PREFIX + runId\n    const commit = await verify(repo, `${ref}^{commit}`, opts)\n    if (commit === '') {\n        throw new Error(`no snapshot ref ${ref} in ${repo} (run predates ` +\n            'snapshots, was pruned, or lives in another clone)')\n    }\n    const tree = (name:string):Promise<string> =>\n        step(`snapshot ${ref} has no ${name}/ tree`, opts, () => run(repo,\n            ['rev-parse', '--verify', '--quiet', '--end-of-options',\n                `${ref}:${name}`], opts))\n    const indexTree = await tree('index')\n    const worktreeTree = await tree('worktree')\n    return {\n        ref,\n        commit,\n        indexTree,\n        worktreeTree,\n        head:await verify(repo, `${ref}^1`, opts),\n        base:await verify(repo, `${ref}^2`, opts),\n        excluded:[],\n    }\n}\n\n// `opts` with GIT_INDEX_FILE removed from the child environment, so an\n// inherited index (inside a hook, say) never replaces a worktree's own.\nfunction withoutIndexFile (opts:SnapshotOpts):SnapshotOpts {\n    const env = { ...(opts.env ?? process.env) }\n    delete env.GIT_INDEX_FILE\n    return { ...opts, env }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66b6d965-2013-4c51-8fbf-1ea833a4f001","uuid":"fe4ac2a8-9d9a-4601-9411-ac6e0055e381","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:08:20.205Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Scope, context, and exploration tools (TS)\n\n`src/scope/` (public surface in `index.ts`), `src/context/`,\n`src/snapshot/`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Every `git diff` argument list starts with `DIFF_CONFIG` (use\n  `diffArgs(...)` in `src/scope/git.ts`); git rejects an empty\n  `diff.orderFile=`, so it is `/dev/null`.\n- Patch output goes through `gitPatch` (streams into a\n  `SectionCapper`), never the buffered runner.\n- `build` takes the git environment as `BuildOpts.env` (the CLI\n  context's env).\n- The secret denylist lives once in `src/snapshot/denylist.ts`; scope,\n  context, and snapshot import it.\n- Repo survey (`scope: \"repo\"`) is `src/scope/survey.ts`: it lists the\n  HEAD tree with `ls-tree` and filters in process (`untrackedPasses`,\n  exact-match linguist set), so the git pathspec is unused there. Every\n  repository-derived string in the manifest goes through\n  `manifestQuote`. The CLI survey branches live in `src/cli/review.ts`;\n  CLI tests are in `test/cli/review-survey.ts`.\n\n## Context\n\n- Every function that runs git or reads files takes a trailing\n  `ContextOpts` (`signal`, `env`); pass the CLI context's env, and the\n  repo env in tests. `pinIndexTree` reads `GIT_INDEX_FILE` from that\n  env, not `process.env`.\n- Blocking git calls use the shared runner; streamed reads use\n  `gitStream` / `gitCapped` (`src/context/git.ts`).\n- Grounding and normalization work on `Buffer`s; decode to text only in\n  `snippet.ts` (model-facing).\n- Exploration tools (`src/context/tools.ts`): `explorationTools(repo,\n  tree, {env})`; each `run(args, signal)` returns a plain object, a\n  model-caused failure is `{error}`, abort rejects.\n- When stopping a `gitStream` early, `await lineReader.close()` before\n  awaiting `done`: a paused stdout keeps the child's `close` from\n  firing.\n\n## Snapshot\n\n- `src/snapshot/snapshot.ts` owns `liveIndexPath` and `copyIndex`;\n  `pinIndexTree` (context) uses them too. Every function takes\n  `{env, signal}`; pass the CLI context's env so `GIT_INDEX_FILE` is\n  read from it.\n- `review.ts` keeps a `durable` flag: until the run record is\n  initialized, the `finally` deletes a captured ref. Code added between\n  capture and `initializeRun` stays inside that `try`.\n- Non-staged reviews read the `pinWorktree` tree even with\n  `review.snapshot: false`; only a pin failure falls back to the live\n  tree.\n- `restore` and `removeWorktree` strip `GIT_INDEX_FILE` from the env\n  they are given (deliberate change 12); other functions honor it.\n- `prune` takes fractional milliseconds: `runs prune` converts the Go\n  duration without truncating, so `--older-than 1ns` stays positive\n  instead of falling back to 30 days.\n- `runs checkout` resolves a relative `dir` against `ctx.cwd`, not\n  `process.cwd()`; CLI tests chdir into the repo, so a test from a\n  subdirectory passes `cwd` to `r.roast` to tell them apart.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Use `newRepo()` (`test/scope/helpers.ts`): a temp repo with its own\n  HOME, XDG_CONFIG_HOME, and `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` file\n  (`repo.globalConfig`, safe to fill with hostile config), passed as\n  `env:repo.env`.\n- APFS refuses non-UTF-8 file names; stage such a name with\n  `git update-index --index-info` to test it on macOS.\n- Memory bounds: plain RSS growth reflects V8 GC timing on discarded\n  pipe chunks, not what code keeps alive. `test/scope/huge.ts` forces gc\n  (`v8.setFlagsFromString('--expose-gc')`, `vm.runInNewContext('gc')`)\n  and bounds `heapUsed + external`.\n- Abort tests put a pid-recording fake `git` first on the env's `PATH`\n  (`wrapGit` in `test/context/bounds.ts`).\n- Tool tests call tools through `call(repo, tree, name, args)` and fake\n  git with `fakeGit` / `onArg` (`test/context/tools-helpers.ts`).\n- Snapshot module tests use the \"messy repo\" fixture in\n  `test/snapshot/snapshot.ts` (copied in `test/snapshot/restore.ts`).\n  A restore failure after `worktree add` is provoked with a hand-made\n  ref whose `worktree` entry is a blob. Tests that check out a worktree\n  remove it with `git worktree remove --force` in `t.cleanup`. CLI snapshot tests turn capture on with\n  `review:{}` (settingsRepo disables it) and read refs with\n  `for-each-ref refs/roast/snapshots/`.\n- `npm run test:one` pipes into tap-spec, which can crash with EPIPE on\n  a failing assertion and hide the summary; rerun the bundle with\n  `node test/one-bundle.js` for raw TAP.\n- Captured-worktree tests build the tree with plumbing (temporary\n  `GIT_INDEX_FILE`, `read-tree HEAD`, `add`, `write-tree`). `write-tree`\n  or `status` on the live index rewrites it, so snapshot the index bytes\n  after those calls when asserting it is unchanged.\n# TypeScript\n\nApplies to `src/`, `test/`, and `scripts/`. Notes for one area are in\nthat area's file (index in `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Tooling\n\n- `npm test` builds `dist/cli.js`, then bundles and runs the tapzero\n  suite; it does not typecheck. A new test module must be imported from\n  `test/index.ts`. esbuild drops unused imports without resolving them,\n  so only `npm run typecheck` catches a broken import.\n- `npm run test:one -- test/<area>/<file>.ts` bundles one test module\n  to `test/one-bundle.js` and runs it through tap-spec. Test modules\n  cannot run directly under Node: their `.js` import specifiers only\n  resolve once bundled. It does not typecheck; run `typecheck` too.\n- Lint with `npm run lint`: it preloads `scripts/eslint-ts6.ts`, which\n  gives eslint the TypeScript 6 API because typescript-eslint throws on\n  the TypeScript 7 that `typecheck` uses.\n- Node runs `scripts/` directly (type stripping), so they use only\n  erasable syntax: no enums, namespaces, or parameter properties.\n- `baseOptions` in `scripts/esbuild-options.ts` holds the esbuild\n  options every bundle shares (text loaders for `.tmpl`, `.md`, `.sh`;\n  `mainFields: ['module', 'main']`, which `jsonc-parser`'s UMD build\n  needs); `scripts/bundle.ts` adds the `require` shim banner. A test\n  that bundles code itself uses both.\n- `npm run build` also writes `dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt`\n  (`scripts/licenses.ts`) and fails, naming the package, when a bundled\n  package lacks an allowlisted `license` field or a license file. A new\n  runtime library must pass it; extending `ALLOWED_LICENSES` needs\n  maintainer approval. `@substrate-system/debug` fails it today, so no\n  `src/` module may import it yet. Runtime libraries are\n  `devDependencies` (bundled); `dependencies` stays empty.\n\n## Source conventions\n\n- Keep source ASCII: write `\\uXXXX` escapes. Some editing tools decode\n  escapes into literal characters when writing; check with\n  `grep -nP '[^\\x00-\\x7f]'` after writing a file. eslint `--fix`\n  (quote-props) rewrites a quoted `'\\u00e9'` object key into a literal\n  non-ASCII identifier; put such keys in a const and use a computed key.\n- eslint rejects control characters in regex literals\n  (`no-control-regex`) and labeled statements (`no-labels`); scan char\n  codes and use helper functions instead.\n- Startup guards live in `src/startup.ts`, not `src/cli.ts`: importing\n  the entry runs the CLI, so testable helpers sit in other modules.\n- Module-level swappable functions use a mutable hooks object plus a\n  delegating export (`terminalHooks`, `skillHooks.lookPath`), because\n  tests cannot reassign an ESM `let` export. Swap the object's field\n  and restore it in `t.cleanup`.\n- Shared helpers; import these, never re-implement:\n  `src/gocompat/` (`strings.ts`: Go TrimSpace/Ext/`%.2f`/strconv.Quote/\n  byte-order sort and `truncateUtf8`; `duration.ts`: Go durations as\n  bigint nanoseconds; `match.ts`: Go `path.Match`),\n  `src/textsafe/textsafe.ts`, `src/fsutil/atomic.ts`\n  (`writeFileAtomic`, options cover trust, credentials, and gate temp\n  names and error messages), `src/git/git.ts` (the only git runner;\n  pass the CLI context's `env`, it reads `process.env` only when none is\n  given), `src/util/pool.ts` (`mapPool`).\n\n// The secret denylist (spec 11, \"Secret denylist\"): untracked paths that\n// are never folded into a review diff, captured into a snapshot, or\n// served from the live working tree.\nimport { goPathMatch } from '../gocompat/match.js'\nimport { git } from '../git/git.js'\nimport { compareBytes, decodePaths } from '../scope/text.js'\n\n// SSH keys match by key-type prefix so suffixed names are covered; a bare\n// `id_*` would also drop ordinary sources such as id_map.go.\nexport const DEFAULT_DENYLIST:readonly string[] = Object.freeze([\n    '.env*', '*.pem', '*_rsa', '*.key', 'creds*',\n    'id_rsa*', 'id_dsa*', 'id_ecdsa*', 'id_ed25519*', 'id_xmss*',\n    'credentials.json', '.npmrc', '.pypirc', '.netrc', '_netrc', '.pgpass',\n    '.git-credentials', '*.p12', '*.pfx',\n])\n\nfunction basename (p:string):string {\n    const i = p.lastIndexOf('/')\n    return i === -1 ? p : p.slice(i + 1)\n}\n\n// Whether a repo-relative `/`-separated path matches any pattern, by its\n// basename or its full path, case-insensitively. A malformed pattern\n// never matches.\nexport function denylisted (\n    path:string,\n    patterns:readonly string[] = DEFAULT_DENYLIST\n):boolean {\n    const full = path.toLowerCase()\n    const base = basename(full)\n    return patterns.some(pattern => {\n        const p = pattern.toLowerCase()\n        return goPathMatch(p, base) || goPathMatch(p, full)\n    })\n}\n\nexport interface DenylistedUntrackedOpts {\n    // Omitted means DEFAULT_DENYLIST; an empty list disables filtering.\n    patterns?:readonly string[];\n    signal?:AbortSignal;\n    env?:NodeJS.ProcessEnv;\n}\n\n// The untracked, non-ignored paths matching the denylist, in byte order.\n// Tracked files are never listed: their content is already in history.\nexport async function denylistedUntracked (\n    repo:string,\n    opts:DenylistedUntrackedOpts = {}\n):Promise<string[]> {\n    const patterns = opts.patterns ?? DEFAULT_DENYLIST\n    if (patterns.length === 0) return []\n    const out = await git(repo,\n        ['ls-files', '--others', '--exclude-standard', '-z'],\n        { signal:opts.signal, env:opts.env })\n    return decodePaths(out).paths\n        .filter(p => p !== '' && denylisted(p, patterns))\n        .sort(compareBytes)\n}\n    fn:(dir:string) => Promise<T>\n):Promise<T> {\n    let tmp:string\n    try {\n        tmp = await fs.mkdtemp(path.join(os.tmpdir(), prefix))\n    } catch (err) {\n        throw wrap('temp dir', err)\n    }\n    try {\n        return await fn(tmp)\n    } finally {\n        await fs.rm(tmp, { recursive:true, force:true })\n    }\n}\n\n// Pin steps 3-7 inside `tmp`: the worktree written through a private\n// copy of the live index, with denylisted untracked paths excluded.\nasync function writeWorktree (\n    repo:string,\n    live:string,\n    tmp:string,\n    opts:PinOptions\n):Promise<Pin> {\n    const idx = path.join(tmp, 'worktree')\n    await copyIndex(live, idx)\n    const excluded = await denylistedUntracked(repo, {\n        patterns:opts.denylist, signal:opts.signal, env:opts.env,\n    })\n    const env = { GIT_INDEX_FILE:idx }\n    // The positive `.` is required: an exclude-only pathspec matches\n    // nothing. `literal` keeps metacharacters in names from widening.\n    const args = ['add', '-A', '--', '.',\n        ...excluded.map(p => `:(exclude,literal)${p}`)]\n    await step('git add -A (snapshot index)', opts,\n        () => run(repo, args, opts, { env }))\n    const tree = await step('write-tree (worktree)', opts,\n        () => run(repo, ['write-tree'], opts, { env }))\n    return { tree, excluded }\n}\n\n// Writes the working tree, as a review sees it, into one unreferenced\n// tree object. Needs no HEAD and leaves the live index untouched.\nexport async function pinWorktree (\n    repo:string,\n    opts:PinOptions = {}\n):Promise<Pin> {\n    const gitDir = await gitDirOf(repo, opts)\n    const live = liveIndexPath(repo, gitDir, opts.env ?? process.env)\n    return withTempDir('roast-pin-',\n        tmp => writeWorktree(repo, live, tmp, opts))\n}\n\n// Records a replayable snapshot: index and worktree trees joined in one\n// composite tree, committed on HEAD (and a differing base), and pointed\n// at by refs/roast/snapshots/<runId>. Throws rather than returning a\n// partial snapshot.\nexport async function capture (\n    repo:string,\n    opts:CaptureOptions\n):Promise<Snapshot> {\n    if (opts.runId === '') throw new Error('snapshot: empty run id')\n    if (opts.headOid === '') {\n        throw new Error('repository has no commits; an unborn HEAD ' +\n            'cannot be restored, so no replayable snapshot is possible')\n    }\n    const gitDir = await gitDirOf(repo, opts)\n    const live = liveIndexPath(repo, gitDir, opts.env ?? process.env)\n    return withTempDir('roast-snapshot-', async tmp => {\n        let indexTree = opts.indexTree ?? ''\n        if (indexTree === '') {\n            const idx = path.join(tmp, 'index')\n            await copyIndex(live, idx)\n            indexTree = await step('write-tree (index)', opts,\n                () => run(repo, ['write-tree'], opts,\n                    { env:{ GIT_INDEX_FILE:idx } }))\n        }\n        const worktree = opts.worktree?.tree ?\n            opts.worktree :\n            await writeWorktree(repo, live, tmp, opts)\n        const composite = await step('mktree', opts, () => run(repo,\n            ['mktree'], opts, {\n                input:`040000 tree ${indexTree}\\tindex\\n` +\n                    `040000 tree ${worktree.tree}\\tworktree\\n`,\n            }))\n        const parents = ['-p', opts.headOid]\n        if (opts.baseOid !== '' && opts.baseOid !== opts.headOid) {\n            parents.push('-p', opts.baseOid)\n        }\n        const commit = await step('commit-tree', opts, () => run(repo,\n            ['commit-tree', composite, ...parents,\n                '-m', `roast run ${opts.runId}`],\n            opts, { env:IDENTITY }))\n        const ref = REF_PREFIX + opts.runId\n        await step(`update-ref ${ref}`, opts,\n            () => run(repo, ['update-ref', ref, commit], opts))\n        return {\n            ref,\n            commit,\n            indexTree,\n            worktreeTree:worktree.tree,\n            head:opts.headOid,\n            base:opts.baseOid,\n            excluded:[...worktree.excluded],\n        }\n    })\n}\n\n// Deletes a run's snapshot ref (the review's cleanup before its run\n// record exists).\nexport async function deleteSnapshot (\n    repo:string,\n    runId:string,\n    opts:SnapshotOpts = {}\n):Promise<void> {\n    if (runId === '') throw new Error('delete snapshot: empty run id')\n    const ref = REF_PREFIX + runId\n    await step(`delete ${ref}`, opts,\n        () => run(repo, ['update-ref', '-d', ref], opts))\n}\n\nasync function verify (\n    repo:string,\n    rev:string,\n    opts:SnapshotOpts\n):Promise<string> {\n    try {\n        return await run(repo,\n            ['rev-parse', '--verify', '--quiet', '--end-of-options', rev],\n            opts)\n    } catch {\n        opts.signal?.throwIfAborted()\n        return ''\n    }\n}\n\n// A snapshot from