{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChM73YTzjQrBJq2qEmGvf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed all three findings, one commit each. The full `npm test` passes (7527 of 7527), and lint and typecheck are clean. One gap: the end-to-end test for the first fix can only run on Linux, so I haven't seen it run yet.\n\n[x] Snapshot capture leaks denylisted secret files whose names are not valid UTF-8\n\n- **Fix:** a new `denylistedUntrackedRaw` in `src/snapshot/denylist.ts` keeps the exact bytes of each name. It checks the name against the denylist after decoding it with replacement characters, so `\\xff.pem` still matches `*.pem`. The snapshot now hands its exclusions to `git add` through stdin (`--pathspec-from-file=- --pathspec-file-nul`), because Node can't put non-UTF-8 bytes in command-line arguments. The excluded list reports the decoded name.\n- **Tests:** a test in `test/snapshot/denylist.ts` uses a fake `git` to list such names and runs on any system. An end-to-end capture test in `test/snapshot/snapshot.ts` creates real files with these names. macOS won't allow those file names, so here that test takes its skip branch, and with no Docker daemon running I couldn't try it on Linux. It will first really run in Linux CI.\n- **Not changed:** `denylistedUntracked`, which `grep.ts` and `list-files.ts` use, still drops these names. That was outside this finding.\n\n[x] `git rev-parse --verify --quiet --end-of-options` breaks snapshots on older Git\n\n- **Test:** a fake `git` rejects `--end-of-options` the way Git before 2.43 does. It reproduced both reported failures, the \"repository has no commits\" error and the failed `load`.\n- **Fix:** I removed the token from both `rev-parse` calls, matching Go. One rev (`--base`) can come from the user, but every rev gets a suffix such as `^{commit}`, so it can't match a git option exactly. I checked that `--since=...^{commit}` fails safely.\n\n[x] Review flag help hardcodes defaults instead of reading src/config/defaults.ts (AGENTS.md contract)\n\n- **Fix:** the turn, survey and quick constants now live in `src/config/defaults.ts`. The help text is built by a new exported `describeReviewFlags(defaults)`, which reads `DEFAULT_LIMITS` and those constants unless given other values.\n- **Test:** it passes made-up defaults and checks that each flag's help shows them. It asserts on help text, which is close to your no-text-assertions rule, but I saw no other way to catch help drifting from the defaults.\n\nI added the reusable lessons to `docs/agents/scope-context.md`, since the root AGENTS.md says area notes go in their area file. My notes are in `.redeye/notes.md`, uncommitted."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":278,"cache_read_input_tokens":99195,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":278},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66b6d965-2013-4c51-8fbf-1ea833a4f001","uuid":"081636d8-858f-4218-9712-9b96c98f131d","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:15:38.100Z","request_id":"req_011ChM73YJKwp22sYyqSjkHV"}
